<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">First Toungoo Empire</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1510">1510</a>–<a href="/years/1599">1599</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as First Toungoo dynasty</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The First Toungoo Empire was the Burmese state founded by the dynasty of Toungoo, which under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tabinshwehti">Tabinshwehti</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bayinnaung">Bayinnaung</a> reunited <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a> in the 16th century. At its height under Bayinnaung it ruled the Shan states, Lan Na, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayutthaya-kingdom">Ayutthaya</a> and Manipur. Overstretched and weakened by revolts, it collapsed by 1599 and was followed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/restored-toungoo-kingdom">Restored Toungoo Kingdom</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-toungoo-empire.jpg" alt="First Toungoo Empire" width="320" height="377" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Soewinhan · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_of_Taungoo_Empire_(1580).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
